title: Tagging from the GUI
tags: [[Hierarchical tags]] GUI
kind: guide
summary: Keys under , (comma) search by a tag, give the selected metarecord one, or take one off — for each of the three tag fields.

Three commands of the shipped `commands.js` ([[User commands]]) tag one metarecord at a
time from the command input, each taking first the field of the tag model it works on —
`tag`, `negative_tag` or `mixed_tag` ([[Hierarchical tags]]) — then the tag, completed
over the paths of the existing ones:

|!Keys |!Command |!Does |
|`, q` `, n q` `, m q` |[[tag:query]] |searches the records having, denying, partly having the tag and what is under it |
|`, t` `, n a` `, m a` |[[tag:add]] |gives the selected metarecord the tag, denies it, marks it mixed |
|`, d` `, n d` `, m d` |[[tag:remove]] |takes a tag of that field off the selected metarecord |

The keys name the field first, then the verb (`a`dd, `d`elete, `q`uery): `, n` and
`, m` are the prefixes of `negative_tag` and `mixed_tag`. The plain `tag`, the one used
most, has the short forms instead of a prefix — `, t` adds it, `, d` takes it off,
`, q` searches it; a prefix `, t` would have shadowed them, since an exact binding wins
over every longer sequence ([[Keybindings]]).

''Adding'' goes through `mf.tag.answer` ([[The metafolder API]]), which applies the
rules of `mf tag` with the same code: the tag replaces the broader ones it implies, takes back the answers it makes
false, and is created — with any missing parent — when its path names no tag yet
([[Tag subsumption]]). ''Removing'' takes back one ref and rewrites nothing else, in
whichever field.

The GUI uses the field names of the convention; the `[tag]` table of
[[CLI configuration]] does not apply to it. To answer many records or a whole folder,
the tagging scripts ask the questions for you ([[Classifying with tags]]).
